  {
    "id": "anno-yanagawa_upper_p195_right-13",
    "type": "Annotation",
    "body": [
      {
        "purpose": "transcribing",
        "value": "大豆合代二萬五千七百二十九兩壹升一合一勺六才"
      },
      {
        "purpose": "modern_jp_reading",
        "value": "大豆合代 二万五千七百二十九両壹升一合一勺六才（印刷のまま）"
      },
      {
        "purpose": "english_translation",
        "value": "Soybeans, total cash equivalent. The printed figure reads 25,729.116 ryo, and I confirmed every glyph at single-character zoom (二 十 九 between 百 and 兩; 壹 升 一 合 一 勺 六 才 after it). Two separate checks on this page both give 25,730.313 instead. First, the note in the next column prints 4.605 ryo per koku, and 5,587.473 x 4.605 = 25,730.3132. Second, 25,730.313 plus the wheat conversion 1,277.71 plus the rapeseed conversion 25,110.093 comes to 52,118.116 ryo, which at the 8 ryo per koku of the 合計 note is 6,514.7645 koku — exactly the amount by which the actual rice (82,242.6765) exceeds the combined rice (75,727.912). The printed 壹升 also has no slot in the ryo ladder (合 .1 / 勺 .01 / 才 .001) that the other two conversions establish. The characters are transcribed as printed and parsed as printed; the editor's note two columns to the right records that this line came from a separate sheet, which is where the discrepancy plausibly entered."
      },
      {
        "purpose": "identifying",
        "value": "大豆合代"
      }
    ],
    "target": {
      "source": "images/upper_p195_right.jpg",
      "selector": {
        "type": "FragmentSelector",
        "conformsTo": "http://www.w3.org/TR/media-frags/",
        "value": "xywh=pixel:1117,1322,80,1838"
      }
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "anno-yanagawa_upper_p195_right-14",
    "type": "Annotation",
    "body": [
